A||||5||88formula||Porting the heads||||1||
Z||000000||88formula||12-12-1999||08:46 PM||||Has any of you fiero owners used the Standard Abrasives do it yourself porting kit <A HREF="http://www.samotorsports.com/diyguide.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.samotorsports.com/diyguide.htm</A>  to Port the fiero 2.8 heads and match the intake runner openings to each other? If you did how did it work and was there any problems with the computer since there is no mass air flow sensor to pick up the extra air the engine will take in? ||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||12-12-1999||10:58 PM||||Outside of just doing the port job wrong, the ECM will see a difference in the manifold pressure at various RPM's and adjust accordingly. In fact, speed density systems (MAP) tend to be more forgiving of changes than mass air flow systems.<P>Make sure you leave the intake vane alone. That is one of the primary reasons for the HO head's increased flow.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||12-13-1999||07:08 AM||||I used an air powered die grinder with a carbide bit to gasket match port the intake manifold and plenums and the exhaust manifolds.  I didn't touch the heads because that would void the warranty on my new long block.<P>The bit cut through the aluminum intake parts very easily.  In fact you have to be careful not to get to aggressive.  The exhaust took a bit longer but it was actually no trouble at all.  The high speed cutter worked great.<P>I've only got about 20 miles on the engine and haven't pushed it yet to see the effect of the porting.  I'll wait until I have broken the engine in a while.||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||12-13-1999||07:48 AM||||I've done some pocket porting on a set of V8 small block Chevy heads with that same kit. In reality, gasket matching the ports does a little bit to improve flo, but not much. The V6 heads are a similar design, so buy a good book about hotrodding heads and you should be ok, just don't take too much material off. In pocket porting, you're mainly smoothing all the rough edges and corners down. It don't have to be polished either. Leave that little vane alone down in the port. It helps flow.||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||12-13-1999||06:29 PM||||Thank you for the info, much appreciated.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fastonpumpgas||12-14-1999||08:34 AM||||Batboy is right, if i remember right it was the intake side that had alot to come out and you just smoth the other, but leave the vein alone.  I woundnt waste my time gasket matching, you might get 2 hp more.  I mean that stuff is good on a 1000hp big block||||reg||1
